          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em invariant measure
            (a.k.a.
            %em stationary
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em steady
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time"} time
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            of the system.
          %p
            An action with an invariant measure is sometimes called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em stationary
            = succeed "," do
              %em steady-state
            %em measure-preserving
            dynamical system.
          %p
            It is an important concept in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamical+systems"} dynamical systems
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+physics"} statistical physics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equilibrium"} equilibrium
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/detailed+balance"} detailed balance
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodicity"} ergodicity
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
