          %p
            In many situations,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measures"} ergodic measures
            even form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            cone.
          %p
            Equivalently, a stationary measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            gives an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+spaces"} probability spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel#measurepreserving_kernels"} measure-preserving kernels
            (see for example at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+couplings"} category of couplings
          %h2#further_properties Further properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An invariant
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measure"} probability measure
                is called
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measure"} ergodic
                if it is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure"} zero-one
                on all
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+sigma-algebra"} invariant sets
            %li
              %p
                A stationary system (for example,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel"} Markov kernel
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/detailed+balance"} detailed balance
                %span.newWikiWord
                  reversible
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/reversible+dynamics"} ?
                if
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi A
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\int_A k(B|x) \,p(d x) \;=\; \int_B k(A|x)\,p(d x) ,
              %p
                i.e. if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is its own
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayesian+inverse"} Bayesian inverse
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equilibrium"} equilibrium
                than just stationarity. (Not every stationary system satisfies this property.)
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+decomposition+theorem"} ergodic decomposition theorem
                says that, under some conditions, an invariant measure is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixture"} mixture
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measure"} ergodic ones
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"}> group
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"}> cone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exchangeability"}> exchangeability
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+set"} invariant set
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measure"}> ergodic measure
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+decomposition+theorem"} ergodic decomposition theorem
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#fritz_definetti
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Fritz"}> Tobias Fritz
                , Tomáš Gonda,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"} Paolo Perrone
                = succeed "." do
                  %em De Finetti’s theorem in categorical probability
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.02639"} arXiv:2105.02639
            %li#markov_ergodic
              %p
                Sean Moss,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"} Paolo Perrone
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A category-theoretic proof of the ergodic decomposition theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.07353"} arXiv:2207.07353
            %li#ergodic_dagger
              %p
                Noé Ensarguet,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"} Paolo Perrone
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.04267"} arXiv:2310.04267
            %li#cornish
              %p
                Rob Cornish,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stochastic Neural Network Symmetrization in Markov Categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11814"} arXiv
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/probability"} probability
